From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:01:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] port 44d8ff4b 3850a79e: serve: GET /v1/load (slots
 busy/decoding, summed tok/s against the highest seen, load_pct and level);
 /v1/load counts what really waits and takes a sustained rate as its 100 %

Squash of the two commits: 3850a79e rewrites most of 44d8ff4b. GET /v1/load (and GET /load, vLLM's
server_load figure) reports load_pct/level/would_wait, slots total/busy/decoding/reading_prompt/free/waiting,
and tok/s against the highest rate held for 10 s with half the slots decoding (STRATA_LOAD_REF_TOK_S fixes it).

Adaptations to v0.2.12:
- GET only, in do_GET. Upstream's POST /load and POST /v1/load (model load, JSON control alias) are untouched;
  RouteTest checks that POST /v1/load still loads.
- _take_control is upstream's, unchanged. Our version's image-gate stand-back (`standing`, `quiet`, the
  image_line checks) belongs to the server image gate (1b9247b1) and comes with that port; load_view reads
  image_line/standing with .get(..., 0) so it is ready for it.
- StrataEngine.load_counts reads upstream's admission state: waiting (control lines), admitting (#1603 slot
  wait), slots_busy, and splits upstream's wait entries [plen, arrival, new, prompt, request]: `coalesced`
  (a STRATA_COALESCE_PREFILL follower holding a preslot) and `resuming` (a wait entry that is not a first
  admission: a read that gave way, a SOLO_AGAIN hand-back to the solo path, a request that found its slot and
  takes the lines again). Those run, so they are not counted as waiting for room.
- The peak file: written only where asked for - STRATA_LOAD_PEAK_FILE, or a <config>.load-peak.json that
  already exists (production's does). Without either nothing is written next to the config (stock behaviour).
- serve/test_load.py: the engine-without-process helper is local (upstream engine state incl. arrivals); the
  image-gate cases go with the image gate port; AgeOutTest (STRATA_IMAGE_HISTORY, dropped) is not carried; a
  new case covers the coalesced and resuming waiters.
- docs/DETAILS.md: the GET /v1/load section (from f2ef22b3), next to the connecting-apps section.

(cherry picked from commit 44d8ff4b52aa56d148741bdef7f260bbec6f4732)
